{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>ואהיה להם</b> — like men who lift the yoke of the wagon: to lift the yoke that is upon their cheek moment after moment." "<b>ואט</b> — like אטה. And the word אוכיל is a noun, like אכל in 'אכל בכסף' (purchase with money), and 'I would bend toward him food.' And R. Marinus said: אכיל is fitting to be אאכיל, like 'ויוסף עוד דוד את כל בחור ישראל' (2 Samuel 24:2), and he interpreted ואט literally, that I would feed gently."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "The clause והייתי מטה אליו אוכיל is difficult; rendered hyper-literally. R. Marinus reads ואט as 'I would feed gently,' taking אט in its sense of 'gentle/soft.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:55.941492696Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}